[1;34mINFO  [0;39m[Claude Code] ## Summary
[1;34mINFO  [0;39m[Claude Code] 
[1;34mINFO  [0;39m[Claude Code] I've successfully resolved both issues by updating the `ParseBenchmarkFactory` class with the following changes:
[1;34mINFO  [0;39m[Claude Code] 
[1;34mINFO  [0;39m[Claude Code] ### Issue 1: NullPointerException in `ParseBenchmark.timeParse`
[1;34mINFO  [0;39m[Claude Code] The problem was that the existing factory method created a `ParseBenchmark` instance but didn't initialize the `parser` and `text` fields that are normally set by the `setUp()` method. These fields are then accessed in the `timeParse` method at ParseBenchmark.java:131.
[1;34mINFO  [0;39m[Claude Code] 
[1;34mINFO  [0;39m[Claude Code] **Solution**: Enhanced the `createParseBenchmark()` factory method to:
[1;34mINFO  [0;39m[Claude Code] - Initialize the `text` field with a minimal valid JSON array `"[]"`
[1;34mINFO  [0;39m[Claude Code] - Initialize the `parser` field by calling the `newParser()` method on the API enum value
[1;34mINFO  [0;39m[Claude Code] 
[1;34mINFO  [0;39m[Claude Code] ### Issue 2: NullPointerException in `ParseBenchmark.Feed.toString`
[1;34mINFO  [0;39m[Claude Code] The `Feed.toString()` method at line 400 iterates over the `items` list, but when a Feed object is created via the default constructor, all fields including `items` are null.
[1;34mINFO  [0;39m[Claude Code] 
[1;34mINFO  [0;39m[Claude Code] **Solution**: Created a new factory method `createFeed()` that:
[1;34mINFO  [0;39m[Claude Code] - Creates a Feed instance
[1;34mINFO  [0;39m[Claude Code] - Initializes all fields including `id`, `title`, `description`, `alternates`, `updated`
[1;34mINFO  [0;39m[Claude Code] - Most importantly, initializes the `items` field with an empty `ArrayList` to prevent the NullPointerException
[1;34mINFO  [0;39m[Claude Code] 
[1;34mINFO  [0;39m[Claude Code] Both factory methods are properly annotated with `@InterestingTestFactory` and the project has been successfully compiled with `mvn install -DskipTests`. The Cover tool can now use these factory methods to generate tests without encountering NullPointerExceptions.
